---
id: org.dxos.review.harness-scripts
name: HarnessScripts
version: 0.1.0
---

A self-review rule: the agentic-review harness reviews its own scripts, TypeScript run
directly with Bun.
This closes the gap where the harness could not review its own diff (the
non-negotiable rules scope to `packages/**`).

## Extensions

| Term   | URI                   |
| ------ | --------------------- |
| `rule` | org.dxos.mdl.rule@1.0 |

## Rules

```mdl
rule harness-script-hygiene: Harness scripts stay dependency-free and honest
  Review the agentic-review harness's own TypeScript for tooling hygiene. These
  files run directly under Bun with no build and no package of their own. Flag:
  a `catch` that swallows an error so a real failure passes silently (as opposed
  to a deliberate, commented best-effort skip); dead or unreachable code and
  unused bindings/exports; comments that restate what the code does instead of
  the constraint behind it (why); a cast to silence the type checker; and any
  new runtime dependency import beyond `node:*` builtins and `bun:*`, since there
  is no package to install it into. Do not flag deliberate, clearly-commented
  tolerations (e.g. best-effort git calls).
  scope: repo
  files:
    - .agents/skills/agentic-review/**/*.ts
  severity: warn
```

## Appendix

```mdl
ext rule
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.rule@1.0
  desc: A machine-checked review rule applied by an LLM subagent or the System One checker.
  inline-prose: true
  fields:
    files:       Glob | Glob[]     # paths this rule reviews, relative to `scope`
    grep?:       Prose             # optional regex pre-filter over file contents
    severity?:   warn | error      # defaults to warn
    scope?:      dir | repo        # glob base: this file's dir (default) or repo root
    unit?:       file | pr         # one verdict per file (default) or per change set
    context?:    ContextKind[]     # diff | imports | importers | siblings | package | public-api | similar | test | pr
    system-one?: on | off          # off when no fetcher can supply what the rule needs
    question?:   Prose             # literal yes/no question for the System One checker
```
